WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.787
This provided script loads sample records into

00:00:02.813 --> 00:00:06.473
the clinic schema Some of the SQL

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.408
uses lookup and join patterns that are

00:00:08.421 --> 00:00:10.329
taught in more detail later so you

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:11.815
do not need to write this loading

00:00:11.829 --> 00:00:15.249
script from memory Run it in the

00:00:15.262 --> 00:00:19.694
browser and inspect the final result Focus

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.852
on what is happening conceptually patients providers

00:00:23.036 --> 00:00:26.512
and services are inserted first The appointment

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.394
refers to existing patient and provider rows

00:00:30.315 --> 00:00:33.091
Appointment-service rows then connect the
appointment to

00:00:33.118 --> 00:00:37.882
services The insert order follows the relationships

00:00:37.895 --> 00:00:42.137
we designed If you use pgAdmin run

00:00:42.163 --> 00:00:43.860
the schema first and then the loading

00:00:43.874 --> 00:00:47.468
script Parent data must exist before child

00:00:47.495 --> 00:00:49.495
rows that reference it can be inserted
